    "scienceExplainedEn": "Sauvignon Blanc is dominated by methoxypyrazines (green bell pepper, grass) and thiols (passionfruit). Chardonnay is a chameleon grape that readily undergoes Malolactic Fermentation (MLF), where sharp malic acid is converted by Oenococcus oeni bacteria into soft lactic acid, producing buttery diacetyl compounds and oak lactones.",
