    "scienceEn": "Bordeaux is divided by the Gironde estuary: 1) Left Bank (M\u00e9doc, Pauillac, Margaux): Deep gravel soils warm quickly, ripening thick-skinned Cabernet Sauvignon into wines with firm tannins, high acidity, cassis fruit, and pencil-lead minerality. 2) Right Bank (Saint-\u00c9milion, Pomerol): Cooler clay and limestone soils favor early-ripening Merlot, producing lush, velvety, plum-scented wines. Matured 12-24 months in French oak barriques (225L) that polymerize tannins and infuse vanillin.",
    "scienceDe": "Die Welt von Bordeaux: Links der Gironde (M\u00e9doc, Pauillac) dominieren warme Kiesb\u00f6den, ideal f\u00fcr die dickschalige Cabernet-Sauvignon-Traube (Cassis, Zeder, kraftvolle Gerbstoffe f\u00fcr jahrzehntelange Lagerung). Rechts der Gironde (Saint-\u00c9milion, Pomerol) dominieren k\u00fchle Tonb\u00f6den f\u00fcr die Merlot-Traube (saftig, Pflaume, samtiger Schmelz). Der 18- bis 24-monatige Barrique-Ausbau im Eichenfass bindet Gerbstoffe und sorgt f\u00fcr das legend\u00e4re Lagerpotenzial.",
