    "id": "tea_oolong_wuyi_dahongpao",
    "category": "tea",
    "nameEn": "Oolong Tea (Tie Guan Yin & Wuyi Rock Oolong)",
    "nameDe": "Oolong (Teilfermentiert, z. B. Tie Guan Yin)",
    "subtitleEn": "Semi-oxidized artisan tea (20-70%); roasted, nutty with orchid florality & dried stone fruit",
    "subtitleDe": "R\u00f6stig, nussig, mit Noten von Orchideen und Trockenobst \u2013 Br\u00fccke zwischen Gr\u00fcn- und Schwarztee",
    "imageUrl": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1576092768241-dec231879fc3?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
    "origin": "China (Fujian / Anxi & Wuyi Mountains) / Taiwan",
    "isImport": true,
    "abv": "0.0% ABV",
    "tasteEn": "Roasted charcoal warmth, toasted hazelnut, delicate sweet orchid aroma, ripe peach, mineral wet-stone finish.",
    "tasteDe": "R\u00f6stig, nussig, warme Orchideenbl\u00fcte, getrocknete Aprikose, samtiger K\u00f6rper, mineralisch.",
    "tasteProfileEn": "Roasted charcoal warmth, toasted hazelnut, delicate sweet orchid aroma, ripe peach, mineral wet-stone finish.",
    "tasteProfileDe": "R\u00f6stig, nussig, warme Orchideenbl\u00fcte, getrocknete Aprikose, samtiger K\u00f6rper, mineralisch.",
    "scienceEn": "Oolong requires master craftsmanship: leaves are withered and shaken in bamboo baskets ('bruising'). Cell walls at leaf edges break down, initiating oxidation while the core stays green. Oxidation is abruptly halted (20-70%) by wok firing ('sh\u0101q\u012bng') followed by rolling and multi-stage charcoal roasting. Gongfu Cha multiple steepings (up to 8 rounds) release successive aromatic layers.",
    "scienceDe": "Oolong ('Schwarzer Drache') vereint die Frische des Gr\u00fcntees mit der Tiefe des Schwarztees. Die R\u00e4nder der Bl\u00e4tter werden durch Sch\u00fctteln gebrochen und oxidieren rotbraun, w\u00e4hrend der Kern gr\u00fcn bleibt. Beim traditionellen Gongfu-Aufguss entfalten dieselben Bl\u00e4tter bis zu achtmal neue Geschmacksfacetten.",
    "scienceExplainedEn": "Oolong requires master craftsmanship: leaves are withered and shaken in bamboo baskets ('bruising'). Cell walls at leaf edges break down, initiating oxidation while the core stays green. Oxidation is abruptly halted (20-70%) by wok firing ('sh\u0101q\u012bng') followed by rolling and multi-stage charcoal roasting. Gongfu Cha multiple steepings (up to 8 rounds) release successive aromatic layers.",
    "scienceExplainedDe": "Oolong ('Schwarzer Drache') vereint die Frische des Gr\u00fcntees mit der Tiefe des Schwarztees. Die R\u00e4nder der Bl\u00e4tter werden durch Sch\u00fctteln gebrochen und oxidieren rotbraun, w\u00e4hrend der Kern gr\u00fcn bleibt. Beim traditionellen Gongfu-Aufguss entfalten dieselben Bl\u00e4tter bis zu achtmal neue Geschmacksfacetten.",
    "culinaryEn": "Steeped Gongfu style in Yixing clay teapots with boiling water. Excellent companion to roasted duck, wild mushrooms, and aged Comt\u00e9 cheese.",
    "culinaryDe": "In kleiner Tonkanne (Gongfu Cha) bei 90\u201395\u00b0C serviert. Hervorragend zu gebratener Ente, Pilzgerichten und ger\u00f6stetem Wurzelgem\u00fcse.",
    "culinaryServingEn": "Steeped Gongfu style in Yixing clay teapots with boiling water. Excellent companion to roasted duck, wild mushrooms, and aged Comt\u00e9 cheese.",
    "culinaryServingDe": "In kleiner Tonkanne (Gongfu Cha) bei 90\u201395\u00b0C serviert. Hervorragend zu gebratener Ente, Pilzgerichten und ger\u00f6stetem Wurzelgem\u00fcse.",
    "faqEn": "Can Oolong tea leaves be steeped multiple times? Yes, premium whole-leaf oolongs yield 6 to 8 rewarding infusions, peaking around steep 3 and 4.",
    "faqDe": "Kann man Oolong mehrfach aufgie\u00dfen? Ja, Spitzen-Oolongs entfalten ihr reichhaltigstes Aroma oft erst beim dritten oder vierten Aufguss.",
    "guestFaqEn": "Can Oolong tea leaves be steeped multiple times? Yes, premium whole-leaf oolongs yield 6 to 8 rewarding infusions, peaking around steep 3 and 4.",
