    "scienceEn": "Historically made by twisting spaghetti strands around a knitting needle ('fuso'). The 3-dimensional corkscrew acts like Archimedes' screw, locking in smooth emulsions, pestos, and cold vinaigrettes that would run off long noodles. Excellent in cold pasta salads because the twisted structure holds shape when chilled.",
