    "subtitleDe": "Eigelb, \u00d6l, Essig/Zitronensaft (Kewpie: Reisessig & MSG); fettreich, seidig, cremig, mild-s\u00e4uerlich",
    "imageUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Mayonnaise_%281%29.jpg/330px-Mayonnaise_%281%29.jpg",
    "origin": "Spain (Menorca / Mah\u00f3n), France & Japan (Kewpie created 1925 by Toichiro Nakashima)",
    "isImport": false,
    "abv": "0.0% ABV",
    "tasteEn": "Rich, unctuous, silky, creamy, mild acidity; Kewpie has intense egg-rich savoriness and umami depth.",
    "tasteDe": "Fettreich, seidig, cremig, mild-s\u00e4uerlich; Kewpie schmeckt deutlich eireicher und intensiver umami.",
    "tasteProfileEn": "Rich, unctuous, silky, creamy, mild acidity; Kewpie has intense egg-rich savoriness and umami depth.",
    "tasteProfileDe": "Fettreich, seidig, cremig, mild-s\u00e4uerlich; Kewpie schmeckt deutlich eireicher und intensiver umami.",
    "scienceEn": "Mayonnaise is a physical wonder: 75-80% oil suspended in 20% water. Egg yolk lecithin bridges hydrophobic oil and hydrophilic water. Kewpie mayonnaise uses ONLY egg yolks (roughly 4 yolks per 500g vs 1-2 whole eggs in western mayo), malt/apple vinegar, and monosodium glutamate (MSG), producing a distinctly yellow, ultra-custardy, umami-rich emulsion.",
    "scienceDe": "Mayonnaise ist eine Wasser-in-\u00d6l-Emulsion: Eidotter-Lecithin h\u00e4lt Billionen mikroskopischer \u00d6ltr\u00f6pfchen in der Schwebe. Die japanische Kewpie-Mayo nutzt ausschlie\u00dflich Eigelb (kein Eiklar), milden Reisessig und einen Hauch MSG \u2013 wodurch sie gelber, dicker und geschmacklich unvergleichlich umamireich ist.",
    "scienceExplainedEn": "Mayonnaise is a physical wonder: 75-80% oil suspended in 20% water. Egg yolk lecithin bridges hydrophobic oil and hydrophilic water. Kewpie mayonnaise uses ONLY egg yolks (roughly 4 yolks per 500g vs 1-2 whole eggs in western mayo), malt/apple vinegar, and monosodium glutamate (MSG), producing a distinctly yellow, ultra-custardy, umami-rich emulsion.",
    "scienceExplainedDe": "Mayonnaise ist eine Wasser-in-\u00d6l-Emulsion: Eidotter-Lecithin h\u00e4lt Billionen mikroskopischer \u00d6ltr\u00f6pfchen in der Schwebe. Die japanische Kewpie-Mayo nutzt ausschlie\u00dflich Eigelb (kein Eiklar), milden Reisessig und einen Hauch MSG \u2013 wodurch sie gelber, dicker und geschmacklich unvergleichlich umamireich ist.",
    "culinaryEn": "Sandwich spreads, base for Remoulade, Tartare sauce, Aioli, Japanese Okonomiyaki, and sushi rolls.",
    "culinaryDe": "Mutter aller kalten Saucen: Sandwich-Spread, Basis f\u00fcr Remoulade, Aioli, Cocktailsauce und Sushi-Rolls.",
    "culinaryServingEn": "Sandwich spreads, base for Remoulade, Tartare sauce, Aioli, Japanese Okonomiyaki, and sushi rolls.",
    "culinaryServingDe": "Mutter aller kalten Saucen: Sandwich-Spread, Basis f\u00fcr Remoulade, Aioli, Cocktailsauce und Sushi-Rolls.",
    "faqEn": "Why does Kewpie taste richer than Western mayo? Kewpie uses exclusively egg yolks (no egg whites) and naturally fermented vinegars with umami seasoning.",
    "faqDe": "Warum schmeckt japanische Kewpie-Mayo so viel cremiger? Weil sie nur das reine Eigelb (kein w\u00e4ssriges Eiklar) und aromatischen Reisessig verwendet.",
