    "scienceEn": "1. Fat Standardization: Whole milk has natural min 3.5% fat (or 'Heumilch' 3.8-4.2%); semi-skimmed has 1.5-1.8%; skimmed <0.5%. 2. Pasteurization: Heated to 72-75\u00b0C for 15-30s killing pathogens while preserving native proteins. 3. UHT (H-Milch): Heated to 135-150\u00b0C for 2-4s. Shelf-stable for months, but caramelizes traces of lactose creating a distinct boiled/cooked flavor. 4. Homogenization: High pressure (200 bar) smashes fat globules into micro-droplets preventing cream from floating to top.",
    "scienceDe": "1. Fettstufen: Vollmilch mind. 3,5% Fett; fettarme Milch 1,5\u20131,8%; Magermilch <0,5%. 2. Pasteurisierung: 72\u201375\u00b0C f\u00fcr 15\u201330 Sek. T\u00f6tet Keime, erh\u00e4lt Proteinstruktur. 3. H-Milch (UHT): 135\u2013150\u00b0C f\u00fcr 2\u20134 Sek. Keimfrei und ungek\u00fchlt monatelang haltbar, entwickelt aber durch Maillard-Reaktion von Laktose den typischen Kochgeschmack. 4. Homogenisierung: Presst Milch mit 200 bar durch D\u00fcsen, zerkleinert Fettk\u00fcgelchen und verhindert das Aufrahmen.",
