    "scienceEn": "1. Sweet Cream Butter: Made from fresh uncultured cream (pH ~6.6). Clean, mild, neutral fat flavor; ideal for baking where acidity is unwanted. 2. Cultured Butter (Sauerrahmbutter): Cream is fermented for 18 hours with lactic cultures before churning. Bacteria synthesize DIACETYL (2,3-butanedione), the signature nutty 'butter perfume', and lactic acid drops pH to 4.5. Beurre de Baratte is churned in traditional wooden or steel barrels, yielding a silky, slow-melting texture.",
    "scienceDe": "1. S\u00fc\u00dfrahmbutter: Aus unges\u00e4uertem Rahm (pH 6,6). Milder, sahniger Fettgeschmack; ideal zum Backen. 2. Sauerrahmbutter (Beurre d'Isigny AOP): Der Rahm reift 18 Stunden mit Milchs\u00e4urebakterien. Dabei entsteht DIACETYL, der aromatische Schl\u00fcsselstoff f\u00fcr den bet\u00f6renden Haselnuss-Butterduft. Fassbutter (Baratte) wird schonend geschlagen und besitzt einen un\u00fcbertroffen samtigen Schmelz.",
    "scienceExplainedEn": "1. Sweet Cream Butter: Made from fresh uncultured cream (pH ~6.6). Clean, mild, neutral fat flavor; ideal for baking where acidity is unwanted. 2. Cultured Butter (Sauerrahmbutter): Cream is fermented for 18 hours with lactic cultures before churning. Bacteria synthesize DIACETYL (2,3-butanedione), the signature nutty 'butter perfume', and lactic acid drops pH to 4.5. Beurre de Baratte is churned in traditional wooden or steel barrels, yielding a silky, slow-melting texture.",
