    "scienceEn": "1. Acid & Temperature: Water is kept at 80-85\u00b0C (bubbles tear the white). Vinegar lowers water pH, accelerating ovotransferrin crosslinking so the outer albumen coagulates in seconds without scattering. 2. Centripetal Force: Stirring the pot creates a vortex that draws the egg white around the heavier yolk into a neat spherical package. 3. Cooking time: Exactly 3 to 3.5 minutes for a tender solid outer white and completely molten liquid yolk.",
