    "nameDe": "Schwarzer Pfeffer (Echter Pfeffer & Tellicherry)",
    "subtitleEn": "Sun-oxidized berries of Piper nigrum, piperine pungency & woody terpenes",
    "subtitleDe": "Fermentierte Beeren der Pfefferpflanze, scharfer Piperin-Kern & holzige Terpene",
    "imageUrl": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1532336414038-cf19250c5757?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
    "origin": "India (Malabar Coast), Vietnam, Cambodia (Kampot PGI)",
    "isImport": true,
    "abv": "0.0% ABV",
    "tasteEn": "Biting heat, woody pine warmth, camphor notes, citrus zest, bold lingering pungency.",
    "tasteDe": "Prickelnde Sch\u00e4rfe, waldig-harzige W\u00e4rme, Kampfernoten, dezente Zitrusfrische.",
    "tasteProfileEn": "Biting heat, woody pine warmth, camphor notes, citrus zest, bold lingering pungency.",
    "tasteProfileDe": "Prickelnde Sch\u00e4rfe, waldig-harzige W\u00e4rme, Kampfernoten, dezente Zitrusfrische.",
    "scienceEn": "Black pepper is the unripe green berry of the tropical woody vine Piper nigrum. After harvest, the berries are briefly scalded in hot water and dried in the sun for several days. Endogenous polyphenol oxidase enzymes oxidize the outer fruit skin, turning it wrinkled and black. The nitrogenous alkaloid piperine (C17H19NO3) triggers TRPV1 heat receptors on the tongue, creating fiery pungency, while essential oils (pinene, limonene, caryophyllene) deliver complex woody aroma.",
    "scienceDe": "Schwarzer Pfeffer wird halbreif (gr\u00fcn) von Hand gepfl\u00fcckt. Beim anschlie\u00dfenden Trocknen in der hei\u00dfen Sonne oxidieren pflanzliche Enzyme (Polyphenoloxidasen) die \u00e4u\u00dfere Fruchthaut runzelig und schwarz. Das Alkaloid Piperin reizt die Schmerzrezeptoren der Zunge (TRPV1) und sorgt f\u00fcr die Sch\u00e4rfe, w\u00e4hrend \u00e4therische \u00d6le (Pinen, Caryophyllen) den warmen Duft liefern. 'Tellicherry' bezeichnet besonders gro\u00dfe, aromatische Beeren.",
    "scienceExplainedEn": "Black pepper is the unripe green berry of the tropical woody vine Piper nigrum. After harvest, the berries are briefly scalded in hot water and dried in the sun for several days. Endogenous polyphenol oxidase enzymes oxidize the outer fruit skin, turning it wrinkled and black. The nitrogenous alkaloid piperine (C17H19NO3) triggers TRPV1 heat receptors on the tongue, creating fiery pungency, while essential oils (pinene, limonene, caryophyllene) deliver complex woody aroma.",
    "scienceExplainedDe": "Schwarzer Pfeffer wird halbreif (gr\u00fcn) von Hand gepfl\u00fcckt. Beim anschlie\u00dfenden Trocknen in der hei\u00dfen Sonne oxidieren pflanzliche Enzyme (Polyphenoloxidasen) die \u00e4u\u00dfere Fruchthaut runzelig und schwarz. Das Alkaloid Piperin reizt die Schmerzrezeptoren der Zunge (TRPV1) und sorgt f\u00fcr die Sch\u00e4rfe, w\u00e4hrend \u00e4therische \u00d6le (Pinen, Caryophyllen) den warmen Duft liefern. 'Tellicherry' bezeichnet besonders gro\u00dfe, aromatische Beeren.",
    "culinaryEn": "Freshly ground at table side over steaks, cacio e pepe pasta, carpaccio, and rich sauces.",
    "culinaryDe": "Immer frisch aus der M\u00fchle mahlen! Klassiker f\u00fcr Steak au Poivre, Pasta Cacio e Pepe, Rinder-Carpaccio und kr\u00e4ftige Schmorgerichte.",
    "culinaryServingEn": "Freshly ground at table side over steaks, cacio e pepe pasta, carpaccio, and rich sauces.",
