    "scienceEn": "White pepper is made from fully ripe red pepper berries. The harvested berries are submerged in running river or tank water for 7-14 days. Microbial fermentation softens and dissolves the outer red pericarp (flesh). The berries are then washed, rubbed mechanically, and sun-dried, leaving only the spherical white-grey core seed. Lacking the terpene-rich outer skin, white pepper delivers pure piperine pungency and a distinct fermented warmth.",
