    "isImport": true,
    "abv": "0.0% ABV",
    "tasteEn": "Paprika: Deep fruity-sweet red warmth. Cumin: Pungent earthy-warm lemon undertone. Nutmeg: Sweet, woody, warm balsamic aroma.",
    "tasteDe": "Paprika: Fruchtig-milde S\u00fc\u00dfe, tiefrot. Cumin: Erdig-warm, unverwechselbar w\u00fcrzig. Muskat: Balsamisch-s\u00fc\u00df, warm, feinherb.",
    "tasteProfileEn": "Paprika: Deep fruity-sweet red warmth. Cumin: Pungent earthy-warm lemon undertone. Nutmeg: Sweet, woody, warm balsamic aroma.",
    "tasteProfileDe": "Paprika: Fruchtig-milde S\u00fc\u00dfe, tiefrot. Cumin: Erdig-warm, unverwechselbar w\u00fcrzig. Muskat: Balsamisch-s\u00fc\u00df, warm, feinherb.",
    "scienceEn": "Gastronomic kitchen chemistry of three essentials: 1) Paprika edels\u00fc\u00df: Dried ripe red pepper pods milled without hot capsaicin placenta ribs; rich in red carotenoids (capsanthin). Warning: Overheating in dry hot fat turns natural sugars black and acrid-bitter within seconds! 2) Cumin (Kreuzk\u00fcmmel): Dominated by cuminaldehyde; essential for Indian curries, Mexican chili, and Middle Eastern falafel. 3) Nutmeg (Muskatnuss): Seed of Myristica fragrans containing myristicin and elemicin oils; always freshly grated into dairy/potato fats where lipid molecules capture the volatile aromas.",
    "scienceDe": "Drei unentbehrliche S\u00e4ulen der Profik\u00fcche: 1) Paprika edels\u00fc\u00df: Aus getrockneten roten Schoten ohne scharfe Scheidew\u00e4nde gemahlen, reich an Carotinoiden. Wichtig: Paprikapulver darf nie in kochend hei\u00dfem Fett verbrennen, sonst karamellisiert der Fruchtzucker bitter!\\n2) Kreuzk\u00fcmmel (Cumin): Gepr\u00e4gt vom \u00e4therischen Cuminaldehyd \u2013 das R\u00fcckgrat f\u00fcr Falafel, Hummus, Chili con Carne und orientalische Eint\u00f6pfe.\\n3) Muskatnuss: Der Samen des Muskatnussbaums; immer frisch \u00fcber die Reibe gerieben in Kartoffelp\u00fcree, B\u00e9chamel, Blumenkohl und Spinat, da Fette die fl\u00fcchtigen Aromen perfekt binden.",
    "scienceExplainedEn": "Gastronomic kitchen chemistry of three essentials: 1) Paprika edels\u00fc\u00df: Dried ripe red pepper pods milled without hot capsaicin placenta ribs; rich in red carotenoids (capsanthin). Warning: Overheating in dry hot fat turns natural sugars black and acrid-bitter within seconds! 2) Cumin (Kreuzk\u00fcmmel): Dominated by cuminaldehyde; essential for Indian curries, Mexican chili, and Middle Eastern falafel. 3) Nutmeg (Muskatnuss): Seed of Myristica fragrans containing myristicin and elemicin oils; always freshly grated into dairy/potato fats where lipid molecules capture the volatile aromas.",
    "scienceExplainedDe": "Drei unentbehrliche S\u00e4ulen der Profik\u00fcche: 1) Paprika edels\u00fc\u00df: Aus getrockneten roten Schoten ohne scharfe Scheidew\u00e4nde gemahlen, reich an Carotinoiden. Wichtig: Paprikapulver darf nie in kochend hei\u00dfem Fett verbrennen, sonst karamellisiert der Fruchtzucker bitter!\\n2) Kreuzk\u00fcmmel (Cumin): Gepr\u00e4gt vom \u00e4therischen Cuminaldehyd \u2013 das R\u00fcckgrat f\u00fcr Falafel, Hummus, Chili con Carne und orientalische Eint\u00f6pfe.\\n3) Muskatnuss: Der Samen des Muskatnussbaums; immer frisch \u00fcber die Reibe gerieben in Kartoffelp\u00fcree, B\u00e9chamel, Blumenkohl und Spinat, da Fette die fl\u00fcchtigen Aromen perfekt binden.",
    "culinaryEn": "Paprika for Goulash and chicken paprikash. Cumin for shakshuka, falafel, and lamb tagine. Nutmeg freshly grated into potato pur\u00e9e and spinach.",
    "culinaryDe": "Paprika f\u00fcr ungarisches Gulasch. Kreuzk\u00fcmmel f\u00fcr Shakshuka, Hummus und Lamm. Muskat frisch gerieben in Kartoffelp\u00fcree, Rahmspinat und Blumenkohl.",
    "culinaryServingEn": "Paprika for Goulash and chicken paprikash. Cumin for shakshuka, falafel, and lamb tagine. Nutmeg freshly grated into potato pur\u00e9e and spinach.",
    "culinaryServingDe": "Paprika f\u00fcr ungarisches Gulasch. Kreuzk\u00fcmmel f\u00fcr Shakshuka, Hummus und Lamm. Muskat frisch gerieben in Kartoffelp\u00fcree, Rahmspinat und Blumenkohl.",
    "faqEn": "Why does paprika turn bitter when frying? The natural high fructose in sweet paprika chars at temperatures above 130\u00b0C; always remove the pan from direct heat when adding paprika!",
    "faqDe": "Warum wird Paprikapulver beim Anbraten bitter? Weil der nat\u00fcrliche Fruchtzucker bei \u00fcber 130\u00b0C verbrennt; den Topf beim Einr\u00fchren immer kurz von der Hitze nehmen!",
    "guestFaqEn": "Why does paprika turn bitter when frying? The natural high fructose in sweet paprika chars at temperatures above 130\u00b0C; always remove the pan from direct heat when adding paprika!",
