    "tasteProfileDe": "Pfeffrige Sch\u00e4rfe, lebendige Zitrusfrische, angenehm herber Biss, feurige Chili-Note, vollfruchtiges Olivenaroma.",
    "scienceEn": "The Levant is the evolutionary birthplace of olive domestication (dating back over 6,000 years). The Souri (named after the historic Phoenician city of Tyre/Sour) and Nabali cultivars are prized for very high oil yields and bold polyphenol levels. Traditional Arab preparation: Green olives are carefully 'cracked' (bruised with a stone or mallet, 'Makbous' or 'Zaytoun Majrouh') to allow brine, fresh lemon juice, garlic, and hot green peppers to penetrate directly into the flesh. Fermented naturally in 10% sea salt brine, maintaining crisp crunch and invigorating sharpness.",
    "scienceDe": "Der Nahe Osten ist die Wiege des Olivenbaums: Schon vor \u00fcber 6.000 Jahren wurden in der Levante Oliven kultiviert. Die Sorten Souri (benannt nach der ph\u00f6nizischen Hafenstadt Tyros/Sour) und Nabali sind weltber\u00fchmt f\u00fcr ihren extrem hohen \u00d6lgehalt und pfeffrige Polyphenole. Die arabische Zubereitung: Die gr\u00fcnen Fr\u00fcchte werden mit einem Holzhammer einzeln angeklopft ('Zeitoun Makbous'), damit Salzlake, Zitronensaft, Knoblauch und frische Chilis direkt ins Fruchtfleisch einziehen k\u00f6nnen \u2013 der unverzichtbare K\u00f6nig jeder levantinischen Mezze-Tafel.",
    "scienceExplainedEn": "The Levant is the evolutionary birthplace of olive domestication (dating back over 6,000 years). The Souri (named after the historic Phoenician city of Tyre/Sour) and Nabali cultivars are prized for very high oil yields and bold polyphenol levels. Traditional Arab preparation: Green olives are carefully 'cracked' (bruised with a stone or mallet, 'Makbous' or 'Zaytoun Majrouh') to allow brine, fresh lemon juice, garlic, and hot green peppers to penetrate directly into the flesh. Fermented naturally in 10% sea salt brine, maintaining crisp crunch and invigorating sharpness.",
