    "scienceEn": "A Tomahawk is essentially a bone-in Ribeye where the intercostal meat and fat have been meticulously scraped away ('frenched') along the entire rib bone, leaving a long bone handle resembling a Native American tomahawk axe. Weighing 1.2 to 1.8 kg and 5 cm thick, it is best prepared via 'Reverse Sear': slow-roasted at 105\u00b0C until the core reaches 48\u00b0C, followed by a screaming-hot sear to develop a Maillard crust.",
