    "scienceEn": "Gyoza are cooked via a two-stage method ('potstickers'): 1) Dumplings are arranged in a hot oiled skillet to fry the flat bottoms until golden brown. 2) Water (often mixed with cornstarch for a crispy lace skirt 'hanetsuki') is splashed in and covered immediately. Steam (100\u00b0C) cooks the wrappers and gelatinizes starch without burning. As water fully evaporates, the remaining oil re-crisps the bottom into shatteringly brittle lace.",
